coder › Done. The `--json` flag is implemented exactly as specified, committed on `work/main` in three small commits (parser, CLI flag, tests), and `bun test` passes.

**Changes:**
- **NEW `src/csv.ts`** — `parseCsv(text: string): string[][]`: empty input → `[]`; splits rows on `\n`, strips one trailing `\r` per row, drops a single trailing empty row; per-row field parsing handles quoted fields (doubled `""` → literal `"`) and unquoted fields.
- **`src/cli.ts`** — imports `parseCsv`, adds the `--json` branch before the usage return (before the final `return`, so `--upper`/`--count` behave as before). Empty input / header-only → `[]\n` code 0; mismatched row → `line N: expected X fields, got Y\n` code 1 with no JSON; otherwise one object per data row keyed by header, all values strings, code 0. Usage line updated to `usage: csvtool --upper | --count | --json`.
- **`src/cli.test.ts`** — added the usage-contains-`--json` test plus all four `--json` behavior tests and the four `parseCsv` tests.

**`bun test` output:**

```
