One small decision beyond the letter of the spec: I kept the `--json` branch after `--upper`/`--count` in the same order as listed and used a `for` loop over data rows for the length check, which matches the "for each data row at index i from 1" wording and makes the line-number check straightforward. The quoted-field parser treats an unterminated quote as consuming to end of row, a detail the spec didn't pin down.
